#+TITLE: EPURE AutoCAD profile returns C0000005 on an unchanged drawing quit
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: native-cad-validation

** Minimal native control
On pfenny, normal interactive Windows account, AutoCAD.Application.24.1
(AutoCAD 2022), create a fresh COM application, wait for quiescence, inspect
the initial document (DBMOD=0), release the document reference and call Quit.
No ALFE, test Lisp, target drawing, runtime trust or file protocol is used.
Temporarily select the existing unnamed profile or Epure before creation;
restore the original profile in finally. Record native PID, creation ticks,
owner SID, kernel handle and natural exit. Never reuse a foreign instance.

| Profile | Native exit | Forced | Error |
| unnamed, no loaded EPURE modules | 00000000 | false | none |
| Epure, initial unchanged drawing | C0000005 | false | none |

A separate visible-window control posts WM_CLOSE to the exact owned AutoCAD
window under Epure; it also exits C0000005 naturally. The corresponding COM
visible-window trial was rejected as transiently busy and forced to clean up;
it is NOT used as successful closure evidence.

** Scope and evidence
This reproduces outside ALFE. It does not identify which EPURE component is
responsible. Loaded native components include DOSLib24x64.arx,
SNCFOutilsARX64.arx, FLSNCFIG.dll and several SNCF DLLs.
Proprietary EPURE sources/PDBs are unavailable to the project maintainer.
Do not blame the ARX's separately established USERPROFILE startup buffer bug
for this shutdown without matching evidence. No vendor binaries are patched.

CI native jobs17691248610 (!507, 4f10bab7) and17691251293 (!476, efb2377f)
pass EPURE API checks and the exact dirty-drawing discard invariant. BricsCAD
COM passes naturally with exit0 in both MRs; BricsCAD batch also passes in
!476. AutoCAD exits BABE variants or C0000005, without forced cleanup.
The lifecycle JUnit records these as failures. A first-chance AV monitor
attached after the test observed no C0000005 exception in one C0000005-exit
trial; its earlier startup was not monitored, so the exit remains unclassified.

** Required resolution
Identify and correct the EPURE profile shutdown defect, or obtain vendor
confirmation of its intended exit contract with sufficient independent crash
evidence. Do not whitelist C0000005/BABE, kill the process as success, or
disable vendor shutdown callbacks merely to obtain a green pipeline.
Keep both MRs unmerged and native qualification blocking.
